@body
# Chapter 3: The Ash Tree

The ash pierced the nine worlds. Its roots drank from [?lore1:lore-check:Josii:unresolved]the Well of Mimir[?].

Odin stood beneath it. "I gave my eye for wisdom," he said. [?q1:question:Josii:unresolved]The line feels flat. Odin should be angrier.[?] His grip tightened on Gungnir.

[?q2:praise:Josii:resolved]Love this image. The tree as both anchor and threat.[?]

Loki appeared from nowhere, as he always did. "Bitter as ever, old man. Did you expect Mimir to hand you the truth on a silver branch?"

Odin turned. The single remaining eye gleamed.

[?q3:rewrite:Josii:unresolved]Fenrir introduction is too abrupt. Build tension first.[?] Fenrir padded from behind the roots.

